{
  "id": "m45l1",
  "title": {
    "es": "Representar un grafo y DFS",
    "en": "Representing a graph and DFS"
  },
  "theory": {
    "es": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Nodos y conexiones"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "Un **grafo** son nodos unidos por aristas. Se representa muy bien con un diccionario: cada nodo apunta a la lista de sus vecinos."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "grafo = {'a': ['b', 'c'], 'b': ['d'], 'c': [], 'd': []}",
          "print(grafo['a'])"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "['b', 'c']"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "La **búsqueda en profundidad (DFS)** explora un camino hasta el fondo antes de retroceder; se implementa fácil con recursión y un conjunto de visitados."
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "Grafos modelan redes, mapas, dependencias, relaciones… son fundamentales en informática."
      }
    ],
    "en": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Nodes and connections"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "A **graph** is nodes joined by edges. A dictionary represents it nicely: each node points to the list of its neighbours."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "grafo = {'a': ['b', 'c'], 'b': ['d'], 'c': [], 'd': []}",
          "print(grafo['a'])"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "['b', 'c']"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "**Depth-first search (DFS)** explores a path to the end before backtracking; easy to implement with recursion and a visited set."
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "Graphs model networks, maps, dependencies, relationships… fundamental in computer science."
      }
    ]
  },
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "m45l1e1",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `vecinos(grafo, nodo)` que devuelva la lista de vecinos del nodo (o [] si no está).",
        "en": "Define `vecinos(grafo, nodo)` returning the node's neighbour list (or [] if absent)."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "def vecinos(grafo, nodo):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "def vecinos(grafo, nodo):",
        "    return grafo.get(nodo, [])"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "grafo.get(nodo, []) evita KeyError."
        ],
        "en": [
          "grafo.get(nodo, []) avoids KeyError."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "function",
          "function": "vecinos",
          "cases": [
            {
              "args": [
                {
                  "a": [
                    "b",
                    "c"
                  ]
                },
                "a"
              ],
              "expected": [
                "b",
                "c"
              ]
            },
            {
              "args": [
                {
                  "a": [
                    "b"
                  ]
                },
                "z"
              ],
              "expected": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "m45l1e2",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `dfs(grafo, inicio)` que devuelva la lista de nodos visitados en profundidad (vecinos en orden).",
        "en": "Define `dfs(grafo, inicio)` returning the list of nodes visited depth-first (neighbours in order)."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "def dfs(grafo, inicio):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "def dfs(grafo, inicio):",
        "    visitados = []",
        "    def rec(n):",
        "        if n in visitados:",
        "            return",
        "        visitados.append(n)",
        "        for v in grafo.get(n, []):",
        "            rec(v)",
        "    rec(inicio)",
        "    return visitados"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "Recursión + lista de visitados; recorre los vecinos en orden."
        ],
        "en": [
          "Recursion + visited list; iterate neighbours in order."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "name": "dfs",
          "harness": "G = {'a': ['b', 'c'], 'b': ['d'], 'c': [], 'd': []}\nassert dfs(G, 'a') == ['a', 'b', 'd', 'c']"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}